  "recommended_report_framing": {
    "careful": "The replicated results do not identify a single uniformly dominant architecture. Instead, they show a tradeoff: MTP has the strongest validation-loss profile, MoE has the strongest test-loss evidence versus dense, dense remains the most efficient baseline, and V3-style routing is directionally useful but not clearly superior to standard MoE.",
    "short": "The 25-seed paired 50M-token analysis shows small but replicated quality improvements for MTP and MoE over the dense baseline, while the dense model remains the lowest-cost model in throughput and memory, with especially large efficiency advantages over the MoE-based variants."
  },
