  "suggestive_claims": [
    "V3-style routing is directionally better than dense on validation loss, but the planned paired comparison does not survive Holm correction.",
    "The global test-loss/perplexity evidence is mixed: repeated-measures ANOVA is significant, but Friedman is not significant at alpha=0.05."
  ],
  "supported_claims": [
    "For validation loss, the four-model 25-seed subset shows a reliable model effect under both repeated-measures ANOVA and Friedman testing.",
    "MTP improves validation loss over dense in the planned paired comparison after Holm correction, with a negative paired mean difference and bootstrap CI excluding zero.",
    "MoE improves validation loss over dense in the planned paired comparison after Holm correction, with a negative paired mean difference and bootstrap CI excluding zero.",
    "MoE improves test loss over dense in the planned paired comparison after Holm correction, with a negative paired mean difference and bootstrap CI excluding zero.",
    "Dense remains the fastest and lowest-memory model among the four replicated models."
  ],
